                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I started playing this game,and I got confused the moment the interface opened. The first thing I did was start the campaign. A good thing because it started learning this game. The problem is it takes a long time to explain what everything means. NUM: n to n, SUM: n to n, sum %2. Even after playing through it all, and eventually finding out what it means. A few moments later, oh yeah, what does this mean again. No tips if you hover above the text. Try to find the right puzzle to find the description again.\n\nThis doesn't mean I don't enjoy this game. I like the concept and the puzzles. Logical thinking and math. I say yes to that. You can get into the game. It's an easy concept but addictive. It's a gem but unpolished. And therefore I do not recommend it (yet)\n\nThe came should be polished, and a lot.\ncons:\nTimer doesn't stop when finished.\nDescriptions and interface confusing. Need more tooltips.\nHints show immediately. It ruins the fun in a logic game.\nWhen finished a puzzle in campaign, no continue in screen, but on top of the screen there is a button, which you always can use\nNo good tutorial.\n\nPro:\nNice concept.\nGetting more challenging over time, because rules change",
